1
00:04:05,714 --> 00:04:11,714
God on Trial is a history, war, drama film directed by Andy de Emmony.

2
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:17,428
In the Jewish tradition of arguing with God, Jewish
prisoners in Auschwitz decide to put God on Trial.

3
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:23,142
Isaac, played by Josef Altin.

4
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:28,857
Ricard, played by Ashley Artus.

5
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:34,571
Moche, played by Dominic Cooper.

6
00:24:34,285 --> 00:24:40,285
Blockaltester, played by Lorcan Cranitch.

7
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Hugo, played by David de Keyser.

8
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:51,714
Schmidt, played by Stephen Dillane.

9
00:36:51,428 --> 00:36:57,428
God on Trial is a 2008 British television play written by Frank
Cottrell-Boyce, starring Antony Sher, Rupert Graves and Jack Shepherd.

10
00:40:57,142 --> 00:41:03,142
The play takes place in Auschwitz during World War II.

11
00:45:02,857 --> 00:45:08,857
The Jewish prisoners put God on trial in absentia
for abandoning the Jewish people.

12
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
The question is whether God has broken his covenant with the Jewish
people by allowing the Germans to commit genocide on them.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
It was produced and shown by the BBC on 3 September 2008.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
Production was supported by PBS, which screened the play
as part of its Masterpiece anthology.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
The play is based on the Elie Wiesel play The Trial of God.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
Cottrell-Boyce describes this tale as "apocryphal".

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
Wiesel later stated that the event was true, and that he had witnessed it.

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
According to Cottrell-Boyce, producer Mark Redhead "had been trying to turn the story into a film
for almost 20 years by the time he called me in 2005 to write the screenplay."

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of holocaust (shoah),
auschwitz-birkenau concentration camp, debate.

20
01:21:54,285 --> 01:22:00,285
The tone is emotional.
